  "reason": "The strongest evidence is that multimodal multiprofile models with weighted fusion and avgpool aggregation outperform single-profile variants, with config_019 (PCA, ResNet50) best at 0.639 accuracy and 0.620 F1; config_025 shows ViT-L offers no clear gain, and avgpool already appears better than transformer for concat. The main untested design choice in this promising regime is RNA representation. config_031 changes only the RNA encoder from PCA to scvi_n200 while keeping multiprofile, ResNet50, avgpool, and weighted fusion fixed, so it isolates whether a learned RNA representation improves over PCA. This is a high-value exploitation/exploration step under a limited budget because it extends the best-performing direction while reducing uncertainty about an important, currently sparse dimension."
